<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramón Herrera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ramón Herrera Rodado</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramón Herrera was a general who served as president of the South Peruvian Republic in 1838–1839, one of the states of the Peru-Bolivian Confederation led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a>. He governed under Santa Cruz's supervision while Chilean and Peruvian forces fought the confederation. Its defeat at Yungay in January 1839 ended both the confederation and his government.</p></div>
